 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Try to think of it as two overlaid shapes, your tent on one side and the main one on the other. Which way do they face? Set it across the door of that flat bit, so you enter into a dry room rather than sitting on top of the door. You can cut it off at the tent site and tape a fresh end. It'll look much better. Set it up so the door opens away from the fire, usually straight out if possible. People who sleep with the door open on a cold night actually get colder. Good. Also, any tree that looks like it might fall on the tent in strong wind should be well away.",
